{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789302673,"nonce":"VqY7PuOCDpQdM7x+Zif/lY7myRE=","title":"A frame in an LLVM-compiled body reports its entry line and hides inlined callees","message":"The Cranelift tier records a source map per body (jit_map::SourceRun with frame chains from Instr::Pos and Function::inline_sites), and the walker reads the same markers, so a throw from a Cranelift body or an interpreted one names the line and every inlined callee. The LLVM tier records nothing: push_jit_frames falls back to the function's entry position for a pc in an LLVM body, and code inlined into it is not named at all.\n\nReproducer: ExcStack.hx -- main on the walker, `for (i in 0...300000) try { t += top(i \u0026 1); } catch (e:Dynamic) {}` so `top` (with leaf and mid inlined) is promoted and then re-tiered to LLVM, then `try { top(7); } catch (e:Dynamic) Sys.println(haxe.CallStack.toString(haxe.CallStack.exceptionStack()))`. --mode interp and --mode jit (before the re-tier lands) print leaf@3 / mid@6 / top@7 / main@13; --mode hybrid prints top@7 (its entry line) / main@13 once `[tier] install findex=230 tier=llvm` has happened.\n\nDesign that fits what exists: attach DILocations to the emitted instructions (a DISubprogram per body, DILocation with inlinedAt built from the Pos site chain -- LLVM models inline chains natively), let MCJIT emit .debug_line/.debug_info, keep those sections' bytes and load addresses in the JIT memory manager, and resolve pc -\u003e (line, inlined chain) with gimli at trace time, the way addr2line does. The AOT binary gets the same for free through the linker.\n\nThe cheaper shadow-frame route (a per-frame position slot stored at every marker, which wasm already uses) costs a store per line in the tier that exists to be fast; not the default.","files":null}]}